-- 141: 80s POP MINING — TUNEPILE HOOKS, REBUILT AROUND A SYNCOPATED KICK.
-- Started as a 120 BPM four-piece groove with hooks mined from ~/tunepile
-- (index/tunepile.db, FTS5). Then the kick was changed to the figure
-- "x x - - x x x - -" (9 steps: hits at 1-2-5-6-7) and EVERYTHING was reworked
-- around it: hats hocket the kick's rests, bass mirrors the kick's hits, clap
-- was dropped, and the arp/melody were re-lengthed to the 9-step group.
--   * arpeggio (d5)  — Tears For Fears, "Everybody Wants To Rule The World"
--       tabs-tidal/Tears_For_Fears_-_Everybody_Wants_To_Rule_The_World.gp4-*.tidal
--       riff as indexed: d5 fs5 a5 fs5 b5 fs5 a5 fs5, extended to 9 for the grid.
--       cutoff sweeps (slow 8, 1600..4400 sine).
--   * melody (d6)    — a-ha, "Take On Me" (1985)
--       tabs-tidal/Emil_Bulls_-_Take_On_Me.gp3-*.tidal (first-note extract).
--       Ramped forward hard (gain slow 16, 0.62..1.15 saw) — it kept getting
--       buried; this is the loudest it gets.
--   * bass (d4)      — Michael Jackson, "Billie Jean" (1983) contour
--       tabs-tidal/Jackson_Michael_-_Billie_Jean.gp3-*.tidal, re-cut to the kick.
--   * pad (d11)      — vi-IV-I-V in F#m (Tunepile chords/progressions), hoRhodes,
--       ramped in (gain slow 16, 0.3..0.62 saw).
-- Claps: tried wet (room 0.45), modulated, then dry — finally DROPPED (d2).
-- Kick: the 9-step "x x - - x x x - -" figure was later DROPPED too (d1 silence) —
-- the groove runs as a skeleton: hats + bass + hoRhodes arp/melody/pad only.
-- Delay: tap/dub delay removed (ddSend 0) from all melodic parts.
-- Sources: bd/hh/ho Dirt-Samples + dubsynth, hoRhodes (project DSP).
-- Mix: per-stream gain deliberate, master UNITY as in 139/140.
-- Verification: recording recordings/jam-20261004-1103.wav with change markers.
setcps 0.5

d1 $ silence

d2 $ silence

d3 $ s "~ ~ hh hh ~ ~ ~ hh ho" # gain 0.42 # speed 1.4 # pan 0.6

d4 $ note "fs2 fs2 ~ ~ cs3 fs2 e2 ~ ~" # s "dubsynth" # waveMix 0.3 # cutoff 380 # fenv 2.4 # sustain 0.3 # gain 0.8

d5 $ note "d5 fs5 a5 fs5 b5 fs5 a5 fs5 b5" # s "hoRhodes" # gain 0.5 # cutoff (slow 8 $ range 1600 4400 sine) # release 0.3 # ddSend 0

d6 $ slow 2 $ note "fs5 cs5 a4 e5 fs5 fs5 d5 b4 b4 e5 e5 gs5 gs5 a5 ~ ~" # s "hoRhodes" # gain (slow 16 $ range 0.62 1.15 saw) # cutoff 4300 # release 0.4 # ddSend 0

d7 $ silence

d8 $ silence

d9 $ silence

d10 $ silence

d11 $ slow 2 $ n "<[fs3,a3,cs4] [d3,fs3,a3] [a2,cs3,e3] [e3,gs3,b3]>" # s "hoRhodes" # gain (slow 16 $ range 0.3 0.62 saw) # cutoff 2400 # release 0.6 # ddSend 0

d12 $ silence
